<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Frost Death Knights</span></h2>Almost every profession is viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic, but some are a bit more powerful than others—particularly for classes that want secondary Stats, like Crit and Haste. This is the case for Frost Death Knights in particular.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Frost Death Knights</h4>Blacksmithing brings with it the additional Sockets we have come to expect, with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55628/socket-bracer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_socketedbracer.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Bracer</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55641/socket-gloves">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_addsocketglove.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Gloves</span></a>, giving a flexible Stat choice that can be very strong. This offers adding more Mastery to your Stat pool, which makes Blacksmithing the best choice of profession when it comes to raiding.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="jewelcrafting">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_jewelcrafting.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Jewelcrafting for Frost Death Knights</h4>Jewelcrafting is often seen as one of the strongest professions, and looking at the various <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76734/serpents-eye">
<img alt="Serpent's Eye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_sc_eyeofacherus_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Serpent's Eye</span></a>
<span class="q3">s</span>, it's no surprise. Jewelcrafters can equip 2 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=83143/fractured-serpents-eye">
<img alt="Fractured Serpent's Eye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Serpent's Eye</span></a>
<span class="q4">s</span> for a big jump in Mastery. While Jewelcrafting is powerful, it does fall behind Blacksmithing due to these Jewelcrafting-specific gems only having single Stats, and it scales worse into the late game when Epic-quality gems are introduced.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Frost Death Knights</h4>Engineering is as close to being mandatory as a profession can be. The power of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> cannot be overstated, as it is essentially an extra trinket that can be used on top of your other procs. It also offers bombs and grenades, which you can use to deal extra damage, as well as a myriad of gadgets.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
